istered and Licensed''. Its accredited provision is concentrated in health, counselling and social-work awards.', 'AMREF Virtual Training School is a private Technical and Vocational College registered by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority under number TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0053/2015, with a licence valid to 28 July 2030 and the register status ''Registered and Licensed''. The register places it in Nairobi County under private ownership. Its accredited course table carries seven TVET Curriculum Development, Assessment and Certification Council awards, all at Level 6, in project management, social work, community health, counselling psychology, environmental technology, health records and information technology, and marriage and family counselling. The provision therefore has a clear health and social-development orientation rather than an industrial trades profile. Because the registered trading name refers to virtual training, e-learning delivery is recorded as implied rather than verified: no learning-management-system or virtual-classroom address could be confirmed while paid search and direct page fetching were unavailable during this pass. The TVETA register publishes no street address, telephone line or institutional email for the school, so those fields are recorded as absent rather than estimated.', '[]', '["Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority (TVETA) registration TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0053/2015, licence valid to 2030-07-28, status ''Registered and Licensed''","TVET Curriculum Development, Assessment and Certification Council (TVET CDACC) assessment for the seven listed Level 6 awards"]', '[{"name":"Project Management (Level 6)","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Social Work (Level 6)","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Community Health (Level 6)","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Counselling Psychology (Level 6)","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name