ssmaking, each approved for a maximum of twenty trainees, which under the schema convention are recorded at Artisan level. Education.co.ke and Teacher.co.ke, both publishing the TVETA register row for TVETA/PUBLIC/VTC/0143/2018, record the centre''s physical location as Kiniu-Kyemuthei off the Machakos-Wote road in Makueni County, its postal address as P.O. Box 65-90301 Ukia, its plot number as NZUUNI/UKIA 221, its telephone number as 0726 410098 and its e-mail address as abcukaatuni.ctti@makueni.go.ke, the county-government domain confirming that the centre is a devolved county VTC. No institutional website, e-learning portal, distance-learning provision or named officer is published in any fetched source, so those fields are left empty rather than estimated.","old_val":"ABC Ukaatuni Youth Polytechnic is a public vocational training centre that TVETA classifies as a Vocational Training Centre (VTC) under public ownership, located in Makueni County in the Eastern region of Kenya. The authority registered the institution on 18 July 2018 under registration number TVETA/PUBLIC/VTC/0143/2018 and its licence ran to 12 August 2030 with the status ''Registered and Licensed'' at the time of the register snapshot of 25 October 2026. The register''s accredited course table lists only tailoring and dressmaking at trade-test level, examined by the National Industrial Training Authority; duplicate register rows for the same two awards were collapsed into single entries, and no other qualification is recorded. Under the Schologic level-normalisation convention, NITA trade-test awards are recorded at Artisan level. No institutional website, e-learning portal, distance-learning provision, campus list or named officer is published in any fetched source, so those fields are left empty rather than estimated.","rationale":"Same register facts (TVETA/PUBLIC/VTC/0143/2018, registered 2018-07-18, licence to 2030-08-12, two NITA trade tests). The staged text drops the ''no address/contacts