tatus ''Registered and Licensed''. The authority''s course table lists Accounting Technicians Diploma (KASNEB), Certified Public Accountants (professional level, KASNEB), and Business Management (craft/certificate level, KNEC). Its official website (https://adeptcollege.ac.ke/) lists its Main Campus at Shawmut Plaza, 6th Floor, Nakuru CBD (phone +254 706 677 132), a Section 58 Campus opposite Optimum Hospital along Kinuthia Mbugua Rd (phone +254 119 927 724), and email info@adeptcollege.ac.ke. Colleges.co.ke also lists it as a private college in Nakuru Town West Constituency, Nakuru County, offering KNEC and NITA certificate programmes.","fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":"Adept College of Professional Studies, which brands its website as ''Adept Institute of Technical & Professional Studies'' and describes itself as nurturing excellence and professionalism since 2014, is a private technical and vocational college registered by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority on 28 January 2016 under registration number TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0003/2016, with the licence running to 8 October 2028 and the status ''Registered and Licensed''. The regulator''s course table for the college lists Accounting Technicians Diploma (KASNEB), Certified Public Accountants at professional level (KASNEB) and Business Management at craft level (KNEC), while the institution''s website advertises Certified Public Accountant (CPA), Accounting Technician Diploma, Accountancy, Secretarial Studies, Full Stack Web Development and Computer Packages. The colleges.co.ke directory places the college in Nakuru Town West Constituency, Nakuru County, and lists NVCET certificate and NITA artisan programmes in electrical installation, fashion design and garment making, food processing technology and information communication technology. The college operates two campuses in Nakuru: the Main Campus at Shawmut Plaza, 6th Floor, Nakuru CBD, and a Section 58 Campus opposite Optimum Hospital 