"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Food and Beverage Management","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Social Work Level 6","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"}],"sources":{"about":["https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0127/2025"],"courses":["https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0127/2025"],"facilities":["http://www.aiu.ac.ke/"],"description":["https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0127/2025","https://maps.google.com/?cid=12302858672577732966","https://odel.aiu.ac.ke/"],"accreditations":["https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0127/2025"]},"facilities":["Library","ICT services","Health services","Cafeteria and student housing","Conference facilities","Sports facilities","Moodle-based ODeL e-learning portal"],"description":"Africa International University TVET Institute is recorded in the TVETA register of accredited TVET institutions as TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0127/2025, registered on 29 July 2025 with a licence valid to 28 July 2030 under the status Registered and Licensed. The register places it in Nairobi County and classifies it as a private technical and vocational college, and its registered name identifies it as the TVET institute of Africa International University. Twenty-six accredited course rows are listed, all examined by TVET CDACC: eight at level 5, four at level 3, seven at level 4 and seven at level 6, covering hospitality and catering, business management, information communication technology, chaplaincy and ministry, counselling psychology, social work, home care and office assistance. The institute operates from Africa International University''s campus at Rhino Park Close in Karen, Nairobi, and shares the university''s library, ICT services, health services, cafeteria and student housing, and its Moodle-based Open, Distance and e-Learning portal, which carries a dedicated TIVET, Professional and Short course ca