00","source_urls":["https://www.atseminary.ac.ke/about.html","https://www.atseminary.ac.ke/study.html"],"stored_value":"Kitale","fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":"Waterworks Road, Section Six Estate, Kitale (P.O. Box 1284-30200, Kitale)","locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"new_wins","rationale":"Auto-sync: sourced teaching-courses correction (False -> True).","decided_at":"2026-11-21T02:13:03.468590+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"has_teaching_courses","settled_at":"2026-11-21T02:13:03.468590+00:00","source_urls":["https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0165/2016","https://www.atseminary.ac.ke/study.html"],"stored_value":[false,"The accredited programmes are theology, chaplaincy, counselling and social-development qualifications; no teacher-training programme is registered on the TVET Authority course table for this licence."],"fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":[true,["Diploma in Theology","Certificate in Christian Ministry","Diploma in Counseling","Certificate in Counseling","Information Communication Technology","Christian Chaplaincy","Counselling Psychology"]],"locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"stored_wins","rationale":"Auto-sync: free-text reworded; canonical narrative kept (reword is not a conflict).","decided_at":"2026-11-21T02:13:03.468606+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"about","settled_at":"2026-11-21T02:13:03.468606+00:00","source_urls":["https://www.atseminary.ac.ke/about.html","https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0165/2016"],"stored_value":"Africa Theological Seminary is a private technical and vocational college in Trans Nzoia County, Kenya, registered and licensed by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority under registration number TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0165/2016. Its accredited programme table lists eight qualifications spanning KNEC craft certificates, a KNEC diploma and TVET CDACC Level 5 and Level 6 awards in information communication technology, social development, counselling, Christian chaplaincy and Christian ministry.","fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":"Africa Theological Seminary (ATS) is a private, non-denominational post-secondary institution on a 20-acre campus in Section Six Estate, Kitale, Trans Nzoia County, registered with the TVET Authority (TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0165/2016) and operating under its parent organization International Christian Ministries on a semi-residential in-service model to train pastors, counsellors and Christian leaders already serving in ministry.","locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"stored_wins","rationale":"Auto-sync: free-text reworded; canonical narrative kept (reword is not a conflict).","decided_at":"2026-11-21T02:13:03.468619+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"description","settled_at":"2026-11-21T02:13:03.468619+00:00","source_urls":["https://www.atseminary.ac.ke/about.html","https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0165/2016"],"stored_value":"Africa Theological Seminary is recorded by the TVET Authority as TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0165/2016, a private institution in the TVC category in Trans Nzoia County, registered on 14 July 2016 with a licence valid to 20 January 2030 and the status Registered and Licensed. The regulator''s accredited course table for the licence lists eight qualifications: KNEC craft certificates in information communication technology and social development, a KNEC diploma in counselling, and TVET CDACC Level 5 certificates and Level 6 diplomas in Christian chaplaincy, Christian ministry and counselling psychology. The seminary''s accredited provision is therefore concentrated in theology, chaplaincy, counselling and social-development disciplines rather than in engineering or construction trades. No institutional website, email address, telephone number, postal address or named officer could be confirmed from a fetched source in this run, so those fields are recorded as null or unknown rather than estimated. No e-learning portal or distance-learning provision is published for the seminary in the sources consulted, and its accredited programme list contains no teacher-training qualification.","fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":"Africa Theological Seminary grew out of International Christian Ministries (ICM), which began teaching seminars in Kenya in 1986 and launched a degree programme in 1993; the name Africa Theological Seminary was given to the semi-residential programmes at the Kitale training centre in 2008. The seminary is registered as a post-secondary institution by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority under registration number TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0165/2016, and most of its study programmes are accredited by the Association for Christian Theological Education in Africa (ACTEA). Its TVETA course table lists KNEC craft certificates in Information Communication Technology and Social Development, a KNEC diploma in Counselling, and TVET CDACC Level 5 certificates and Level 6 diplomas in Christian Chaplaincy, Christian Ministry and Counselling Psychology, while the seminary''s own study page lists Theology and Counseling programmes at certificate and diploma level. ATS trains leaders ''in ministry'' rather than ''for ministry'': all programmes run on an in-service model built around block courses so students can continue serving in their primary ministries while studying. The institution sits on 20 acres of self-owned land on Waterworks Road in Section Six Estate, about 1.5 km from Kitale town''s central business district, with dormitories, a 30,000-item library, a computer laboratory and a chapel hall on site.","locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"merge","rationale":"Auto-sync: deterministic non-destructive array/course union.","decided_at":"2026-11-21T02:13:03.468626+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_p