n Trans Nzoia County, registered on 14 July 2016 with a licence valid to 20 January 2030 and the status Registered and Licensed. The regulator''s accredited course table for the licence lists eight qualifications: KNEC craft certificates in information communication technology and social development, a KNEC diploma in counselling, and TVET CDACC Level 5 certificates and Level 6 diplomas in Christian chaplaincy, Christian ministry and counselling psychology. The seminary''s accredited provision is therefore concentrated in theology, chaplaincy, counselling and social-development disciplines rather than in engineering or construction trades. No institutional website, email address, telephone number, postal address or named officer could be confirmed from a fetched source in this run, so those fields are recorded as null or unknown rather than estimated. No e-learning portal or distance-learning provision is published for the seminary in the sources consulted, and its accredited programme list contains no teacher-training qualification.', '["20-acre self-owned campus with permanent buildings","Two furnished office blocks with 24-hour internet access","Four lecture rooms","Library with over 30,000 study and research materials","Textbook centre","Computer laboratory with over 10 internet-connected computers","Prayer tower for private prayer and meditation","Dining hall and kitchen","Student dormitories and hostels","Guest houses for visiting faculty, speakers and church leaders","Carpentry workshop producing furniture on order","Canteen and bookstore","Chapel hall for worship and large gatherings","Own water borehole","24-hour automatic standby generator","Football field and volleyball court"]', '["TVETA","KNEC","TVET CDACC","Association for Christian Theological Education in Africa (ACTEA) accreditation of most study programmes"]', '[{"name":"Theology","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Theology","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":