y":"unknown"},{"name":"TV & Film Production","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"unknown"},{"name":"Acting for Film, TV & Theatre","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"unknown"},{"name":"Acting for Film, TV & Theatre","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"unknown"},{"name":"Animation & VFX","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"unknown"},{"name":"Animation & VFX","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"unknown"},{"name":"Radio Production","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"unknown"},{"name":"Radio Production","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"unknown"},{"name":"Music & Artist Development","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"unknown"}],"sources":{"about":"https://afttti.co.ke/","courses":"https://afttti.co.ke/","facilities":"https://afttti.co.ke/about","description":"https://afttti.co.ke/","accreditations":"https://afttti.co.ke/about"},"facilities":["Ambar House, 3rd Floor, Baricho Road, Nairobi campus","Hands-on film, television and radio production equipment with class sizes of 15-30 students"],"description":"The Africa Film and Television Talent Training Institute is a TVETA-accredited creative-arts college based at Ambar House on Baricho Road in Nairobi. Its published programme list is level-structured: TV and Film Production, Acting for Film, TV and Theatre, Animation and VFX and Radio Production are each offered at both diploma and certificate level, while Music and Artist Development is published as a diploma. The institute states that its comprehensive programmes run for 18 months with class sizes of 15 to 30 students, and that graduates leave with a professional portfolio from its learn-as-you-do production model. It also advertises TVETA accreditation and ICM (UK) approval, and runs a holiday creative-arts bootcamp for ages 6 to 18.","accreditations":["TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0166/2016","ICM (UK) approved centre"]},"basic_info":{"email":"info@afttti.co.ke","phone":"+254 729 653 209","sources":{"email":"https://afttti.co.ke/about","phone":"https://afttti.co.ke/about","website":"https://afttti.