ma Campus is a private technical and vocational college campus in Bungoma County, Western region, Kenya, registered and licensed by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority as TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0088/2016 and accredited for KASNEB and KNEC business, accountancy, human resource, information technology, social development and supply chain programmes at craft and diploma level.","fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":"African Institute of Research and Development Studies - Bungoma Campus is a private technical and vocational college campus in Bungoma County, Western region, Kenya, registered and licensed by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority as TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0088/2016 and accredited for KASNEB and KNEC business, accountancy, human resource, information technology, social development and supply chain programmes at craft and diploma levels. The campus operates from College Plaza, 3rd Floor, opposite Main Stage, Bungoma Town, and belongs to the AIRADS College network of campuses.","locked_by_verification":true},{"settled":true,"decision":"stored_wins","rationale":"Auto-sync: free-text reworded; canonical narrative kept (reword is not a conflict).","decided_at":"2026-11-21T17:45:09.481346+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"description","settled_at":"2026-11-21T17:45:09.481346+00:00","source_urls":["https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0088/2016","https://www.airads.ac.ke/contact/","https://studyinkenya.co.ke/campus/african-institute-of-research-and-development-studies/bungoma-town-campus","https://portal.airads.ac.ke/Home/Login?v1=639307360825094079"],"stored_value":"The African Institute of Research and Development Studies - Bungoma Campus is the Bungoma Town campus of AIRADS College, a private technical and vocational college registered by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority under registration number TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0088/2016, registered on 14 April 2016 with a licence valid to 2 July 2029 in the Registered and Licensed status. The register''s accredited table carries twelve rows which de-duplicate to ten distinct awards: KASNEB craft information communication technology and the Accounting Technicians Diploma, KNEC craft certificates in accountancy, business management, social development, human resource management, information communication technology and supply chain management, and KNEC diplomas in business management and human resource management, with craft recorded as Certificate and diplomas as Diploma. The college''s own website at airads.ac.ke lists Bungoma Town Campus among its seven campuses, giving its address as College Plaza, 3rd Floor, opposite Main Stage, Bungoma, and its dedicated telephone line as 0715 771 316, alongside the head office at Institute Plaza, 3rd Floor, on 0723 555 999 and info@airads.ac.ke. Study in Kenya independently lists the Bungoma Town Campus in Bungoma County within the AIRADS College campus network that also covers Eldoret, Nairobi City, Kericho, Kisumu, Nakuru, Mombasa, Lodwar and Maralal, which confirms that the campus is a branch of the multi-campus college rather than a separately registered institution. No e-learning portal specific to this campus, distance-learning provision, student population figure or named campus officer is published, so those fields remain empty rather than estimated.","fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":"The African Institute of Research and Development Studies - Bungoma Campus is the Bungoma Town campus of AIRADS College, a private technical and vocational college registered by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority under registration number TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0088/2016, registered on 14 April 2016 with a licence valid to 2 July 2029 in the Registered and Licensed status. The register''s accredited programme records for the campus list eleven course rows covering the KASNEB craft Information Communication Technology award and the Accounting Technicians Diploma alongside a KASNEB Certified Public Accountants professional stream, and KNEC-examined craft certificates and diplomas in accountancy, business management, human resource management, information communication technology, social development and supply chain management. The campus operates from College Plaza, 3rd Floor, opposite Main Stage in Bungoma Town, and the AIRADS College network lists Bungoma Town alongside Eldoret, Nairobi, Kericho, Kisumu, Nakuru and Mombasa campus locations. Contact is maintained on 0715 771316, and the college runs a student portal at portal.airads.ac.ke; no dedicated e-learning platform or distance-learning provision is published for the campus.","locked_by_verification":true}]', 'flagged', null, 'e8e12407c287', null, null, null, 1, null, 'verification', null, null, 'register', 'verification re-research: website, email, logo_url, location (run e8e12407c287)', '2026-11-09 01:11:05.700539+00', 'verification', 1, 2, 0, null, null, '["implied","AIRADS runs a student portal at portal.airads.ac.ke (login page cached; powered by Optimum Computer Systems Limited) - a generic student/ERP sign-in portal, not a published LMS; no moodle or e-learning platform URL is published for the campus."]', '["none","No distance, open or online learning provision is published; the TVETA record lists campus-based programmes only."]', '[true,"Information Communication Technology (Craft); Accounting Technicians Diploma; Accountancy (Craft); Business Management (Craft); Business Management (Diploma); Human Resource Management (Craft); Supply Chain Management (Craft)"]', '["Bungoma Town Campus - College Plaza, 3rd Floor, opposite Main Stage, Bungoma Town"]', '["African Institute of Research and Development Studies (AIRADS College)"]', 'African Institute of Research and Development Studies - Bungoma Campus is a private technical and vocational college campus in Bungoma County, Western region, Kenya, registered and licensed by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority as TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0088/2016 and accredited for KASNEB and KNEC business, accountancy, human resource, information technology, social development and supply chain programmes at craft and diploma level.', 'The African Institute of Research and Development Studies - Bungoma Campus is the Bungoma Town campus of AIRADS College, a private technical and vocational college registered by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority under registration number TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0088/2016, registered on 14 April 2016 with a licence valid to 2 July 2029 in the Registered and Licensed status. The register''s accredited table carries twelve rows which de-duplicate to ten distinct awards: KASNEB craft information communication technology and the Accounting Technicians Diploma, KNEC craft certificates in accountancy, business management, social development, human resource management, information communication technology and supply chain management, and KNEC diplomas in business management and human resource management, with craft recorded as Certificate and diplomas as Diploma. The college''s own website at airads.ac.ke lists Bungoma Town Campus among its seven campuses, giving its address as College Plaza, 3rd Floor, opposite Main Stage, Bungoma, and its dedicated telephone line as 0715 771 316, alongside the head office at Institute Plaza, 3rd Floor, on 0723 555 999 and info@airads.ac.ke. Study in Kenya independently lists the Bungoma Town Campus in Bungoma County within the AIRADS College campus network that also covers Eldoret, Nairobi City, Kericho, Kisumu, Nakuru, Mombasa, Lodwar and Maralal, which confirms that the campus is a branch of the multi-campus college rather than a separately registered institution. No e-learning portal specific to this campus, distance-learning provision, student population figure or named campus officer is published, so those fields remain empty rather than estimated.', '[]', '["TVETA registration TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0088/2016, registered 2016-04-14, licence expiry 2029-07-02, status ''Registered and Licensed''","Kenya Accountants and Secretaries National Examinations Board (KASNEB) examinations for the accounting technicians diploma and craft information communication technology","Kenya National Examinations Council (KNEC) examinations for the craft and diploma business programmes"]', '[{"name":"Information Communication Technology (Craft, KASNEB)","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KASNEB"},{"name":"Accounting Technicians Diploma","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"KASNEB"},{"name":"Accountancy (Craft)","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Business Management (Craft)","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Social Development (Craft)","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Human Resource Management (Craft)","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Information Communication Technology (Craft, KNEC)","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Supply Chain Management (Craft)","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Business Management (Diploma)","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Human Resource Management (Diploma)","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"KNEC"}]', '[]', 78, '{"town":{"run_id":"e8e12407c287","status":"confirmed","rationale":"town (''Bungoma'') corroborated in cached evidence.","source_url":"https://studyinkenya.co.ke/campus/african-institute-of-research-and-development-studies/bungoma-town-campus","url_checked":"https://studyinkenya.co.ke/campus/african-institute-of-research-and-development-studies/bungoma-town-campus","verified_at":"2026-11-21T17:45:10.273245+00:00"},"type":{"run_id":"e8e12407c287","status":"confirmed","rationale":"TVETA corpus entry TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0088/2016 confirms TVET institution.","source_url":"https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0088/2016","url_checked":"https://www.tveta.go.ke/ins