,"proposed_value":["implied","The institute runs a student portal at portal.airads.ac.ke/Home/Login titled ''AFRICAN INSTITUTE OF RESEARCH AND DEVELOPMENT STUDIES PORTAL'' (powered by Optimum Computer Systems Limited), but it is a generic student/ERP sign-in with admission-letter download and course listings; no dedicated LMS (moodle, e-learning, canvas) URL was found, so e-learning is implied rather than verified."],"locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"new_wins","rationale":"Auto-sync: sourced teaching-courses correction (False -> True).","decided_at":"2026-11-21T02:50:30.184102+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"has_teaching_courses","settled_at":"2026-11-21T02:50:30.184102+00:00","source_urls":["https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0137/2024"],"stored_value":[false,"The accredited programmes are social work, community development, nutrition, agripreneurship, community health and information technology courses; no teacher-training programme is listed."],"fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":[true,["Social Work and Community Development","Information Communication Technology","Nutrition and Dietetics","Social Development","Agripreneurship","Community Health"]],"locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"stored_wins","rationale":"Auto-sync: free-text reworded; canonical narrative kept (reword is not a conflict).","decided_at":"2026-11-21T02:50:30.184109+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"about","settled_at":"2026-11-21T02:50:30.184109+00:00","source_urls":["https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0137/2024","https://airads.ac.ke/contact/"],"stored_value":"African Institute of Research and Development Studies Maralal is the Samburu County campus of the private African Institute of Research and Development Studies chain, located at Maralal in the Rift Valley region, Kenya. It is registered and licensed by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority as TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0137/2024 and trains in social work, community development, nutrition, agripreneurship and community health.","fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":"African Institute of Research and Development Studies (AIRADS) Maralal is the Samburu County campus of the private AIRADS College chain. It operates as Maralal Town Campus in the Supa Sacco Building, 2nd Floor, opposite Huduma Centre in Maralal town, and is registered by TVETA under TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0137/2024, training in social work and community development, information communication technology, nutrition and dietetics, agripreneurship and community health.","locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"stored_wins","rationale":"Auto-sync: free-text reworded; canonical narrative kept (reword is not a conflict).","decided_at":"2026-11-21T02:50:30.184116+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"description","settled_at":"2026-11-21T02:50:30.184116+00:00","source_urls":["https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0137/2024","https://airads.ac.ke/contact/","https://www.facebook.com/people/Airads-college-maralal/61551590921513/"],"stored_value":"African Institute of Research and Development Studies Maralal is a private technical and vocational college registered by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority on 29 October 2024 under registration number TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0137/2024, with a licence valid to 28 October 2029 in ''Registered and Licensed'' status; the regulator records its category as TVC and its county as Samburu. The TVETA accredited course table lists eight qualifications: KNEC craft programmes in social development, information communication technology and nutrition and dietetics; KNEC diplomas in social work and community development and in nutrition and dietetics; and TVET CDACC competency-based programmes in agripreneurship at Level 4 and Level 5 and community health at Level 5. The register shows the same institute group operating other branches elsewhere in Kenya, including campuses recorded in Nakuru, Kericho, Lodwar, Kisumu, Bungoma, Nairobi, Eldoret and Mombasa, so programme availability at the Maralal branch should be confirmed with the campus itself. Its locality is taken from the institution name recorded by the regulator, which places the campus at Maralal in Samburu County within the Rift Valley region. The institute group''s website publishes contact lines for the campuses, and the group''s WEB-contacts page carries the campus line printed here; no email address is published for the Maralal campus on the fetched pages.","fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":"African Institute of Research and Development Studies Maralal is a private technical and vocational college registered by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority on 29 October 2024 under registration number TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0137/2024, with a licence valid to 28 October 2029 in ''Registered and Licensed'' status; the regulator records its category as TVC and its county as Samburu. The campus trades as Maralal Town Campus and sits in the Supa Sacco Building, 2nd Floor, opposite Huduma Centre in Maralal town, sharing the group head-office contacts at info@airads.ac.ke and the campus line 0717 885 888. The TVETA accredited course table lists eight qualifications: KNEC craft programmes in social development, information communication technology and nutrition and dietetics; KNEC diplomas in social work and community development and in nutrition and dietetics; and TVET CDACC competency-based programmes in agripreneurship (Levels 4 and 5) and community health (Level 5). The campus is part of the AIRADS College chain, which also operates campuses in Eldoret, Nakuru, Kisumu, Kericho, Bungoma, Lodwar and Nairobi under the website www.airads.ac.ke, and its students use the group student portal at portal.airads.ac.ke. Its Facebook presence (''Airads college maralal'', about 672 likes, and ''Airads College Maralal Campus'') advertises professional short courses, computer packages, diploma, certificate and artisan programmes to the Maralal community.","locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"merge","rationale":"Auto-sync: deterministic non-destructive array/course union.","decided_at":"2026-11-21T02:50:30.184171+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"courses","settled_at":"2026-11-21T02:50:30.184171+00:00","source_urls":["https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0137/2024"],"merged_value":[{"name":"Social Development","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Information Communication Technology","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Nutrition and Dietetics","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Nutrition and Dietetics","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Agripreneurship Level 4","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Agripreneurship Level 5","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Community Health Level 5","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Social Development (Craft)","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Social Work and Community Development","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Information Communication Technology (Craft)","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Nutrition and Dietetics (Craft)","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Nutrition and Dietetics (Diploma)","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Agripreneurship Level 4","level":"Artisan","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Agripreneurship Level 5","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Community Health Level 5","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"}],"stored_value":[{"name":"Social Development (Craft)","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name":"Social Work and Community Development","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"KNEC"},{"name