 fetched this run) matches that exact name and registration number and further places the college at Minoki Building on Oginga Odinga Street in Kisumu (plot BLOCK 7/198), with postal address P.O. Box 9324-40141 Kisumu and telephone 0722747971; these are the location, town and phone values recorded here, and no official website or email address could be confirmed on any fetched source, so those fields remain null. Its accredited programme table lists sixteen rows, of which fifteen are reproduced here as distinct qualifications: the Certified Public Accountants professional row is omitted because it does not map to a canonical level in the vocabulary. Seven craft certificates and seven diplomas are examined by KNEC in business, human resource management, information communication technology, sales and marketing, social development, supply chain management, tourism and tour guiding, and one diploma is examined by KASNEB as the Accounting Technicians Diploma. No competency-based TVET CDACC or NITA provision appears on the register entry. The institute operates other separately registered branches under the same registered name in Nakuru, Kericho, Lodwar, Mombasa (deregistered), Bungoma, Nairobi and Eldoret, so the Kisumu entity is a distinct registrant from the wider AIRADS network.","accreditations":["TVETA registration TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0059/2018, registered 2018-04-12, licence valid to 2028-10-03, status ''Registered and Licensed''","KNEC craft and diploma examinations","KASNEB examinations for the Accounting Technicians Diploma"]},"sources":{"type":"https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0059/2018","about":"https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0059/2018","email":["https://www.airads.ac.ke/contact/"],"phone":"https://education.co.ke/african-institute-of-research-and-development-studies-kisumu-courses-offered-contacts-application-procedure/","courses":"https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?detail