moodle, lms, e-learning, canvas) is published, so this is a generic student portal, not verified e-learning."],"locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"new_wins","rationale":"Auto-sync: sourced teaching-courses correction (False -> True).","decided_at":"2026-11-21T12:14:31.556834+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"has_teaching_courses","settled_at":"2026-11-21T12:14:31.556834+00:00","source_urls":["https://catic.co.ke/","https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0138/2024"],"stored_value":[false,"The accredited programmes are agricultural production, agripreneurship and apiculture courses at TVET CDACC Levels 3 to 5; no teacher-training programme is registered."],"fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":[true,["Horticulture Level 3","Dairy Farm Attendance Level 4","General Agriculture Level 4","Agriculture and Extension Level 5","Sustainable Agriculture for Rural Development Level 5","Apiculture Level 5"]],"locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"merge","rationale":"Auto-sync: deterministic non-destructive array/course union.","decided_at":"2026-11-21T12:14:31.556958+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"campuses","settled_at":"2026-11-21T12:14:31.556958+00:00","source_urls":["https://www.cheptebo.org/","https://catic.co.ke/"],"merged_value":["Cheptebo Agricultural Training and Innovation Centre (CATIC) — Kerio Valley, Keiyo South","Cheptebo Agricultural Training and Innovation Centre (CATIC) - Keiyo South, Soy North Ward, on the C51 Iten-Kabarnet road near Cheploch Gorge, Kerio Valley"],"stored_value":["Cheptebo Agricultural Training and Innovation Centre (CATIC) — Kerio Valley, Keiyo South"],"fact_check_url":null,"merge_proposal":["Cheptebo Agricultural Training and Innovation Centre (CATIC) — Kerio Valley, Keiyo South","Cheptebo Agricultural Training and Innovation Centre (CATIC) - Keiyo South, Soy North Ward, on the C51 Iten-Kabarnet road near Cheploch Gorge, Kerio Valley"],"proposed_value":["Cheptebo Agricultural Training and Innovation Centre (CATIC) - Keiyo South, Soy North Ward, on the C51 Iten-Kabarnet road near Cheploch Gorge, Kerio Valley"],"locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"stored_wins","rationale":"Auto-sync: free-text reworded; canonical narrative kept (reword is not a conflict).","decided_at":"2026-11-21T12:14:31.557183+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"about","settled_at":"2026-11-21T12:14:31.557183+00:00","source_urls":["https://www.cheptebo.org/","https://catic.co.ke/","https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0138/2024"],"stored_value":"AIC Cheptebo Agricultural and Innovation Centre is a private TVET institution in the Kerio Valley of Elgeyo Marakwet County, Kenya, registered and licensed by the Technical and Vocational Education and Training Authority as TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0138/2024. It provides practical agricultural training through the Cheptebo Agricultural Training and Innovation Centre (CATIC), a ministry of the Africa Inland Church Kenya established in 1986.","fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":"AIC Cheptebo Agricultural and Innovation Centre is a private TVET institution in the Kerio Valley, Elgeyo Marakwet County, registered by TVETA as TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0138/2024. It operates as the Cheptebo Agricultural Training and Innovation Centre (CATIC), a ministry of Africa Inland Church Kenya established in 1986, delivering accredited agricultural courses from Level 3 to Level 5 on a 20-hectare demonstration farm.","locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"stored_wins","rationale":"Auto-sync: free-text reworded; canonical narrative kept (reword is not a conflict).","decided_at":"2026-11-21T12:14:31.557201+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"description","settled_at":"2026-11-21T12:14:31.557201+00:00","source_urls":["https://www.cheptebo.org/","https://www.cheptebo.org/about-us.php","https://www.cheptebo.org/contact.php","https://catic.co.ke/","https://www.tveta.go.ke/institution-details/?details=TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0138/2024"],"stored_value":"AIC Cheptebo Agricultural and Innovation Centre is registered by the TVET Authority as TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0138/2024, a private Technical and Vocational College in the TVC category in Elgeyo Marakwet County, registered on 29 October 2024 with a licence valid to 28 October 2029 and the status Registered and Licensed. The institution operates as the Cheptebo Agricultural Training and Innovation Centre, which its own website describes as providing practical training courses in agricultural production with a particular focus on semi-arid areas, and which held its first graduation ceremony on 6 December 2026. The regulator''s accredited course table carries eighteen entries made up largely of duplicated CDACC rows; once duplicates are collapsed it resolves to nine accredited TVET CDACC qualifications spanning Levels 3 to 5: horticulture and poultry kienyeji operator at Level 3, agriculture extension at Level 4, and horticulture, integrated pest management, poultry breeding operations, sustainable agriculture for rural development, agripreneurship and apiculture at Level 5. The wider Cheptebo Rural Development Centre site, a ministry of the Africa Inland Church Kenya established in 1986, publishes a 20-hectare demonstration and training farm, a conference centre with four halls and residential accommodation for 100 guests, a KEPHIS-certified tree nursery and a fruit processing factory supported by the Government of Japan. No institutional email address or telephone number for the centre was confirmed from a page fetched in this run, and the imported town value was a plus-code string with no fetched corroboration, so both remain unverified.","fact_check_url":null,"proposed_value":"AIC Cheptebo Agricultural and Innovation Centre is registered by the TVET Authority as TVETA/PRIVATE/TVC/0138/2024, a private Technical and Vocational College (TVC category) in Elgeyo Marakwet County, Kenya, with the status Registered and Licensed. It operates as the Cheptebo Agricultural Training and Innovation Centre (CATIC), a ministry of Africa Inland Church Kenya established in 1986 and governed by a Board of Management drawn from the church, local leaders and community representatives. CATIC is located in Keiyo South Constituency, Soy North Ward, on the C51 Iten-Kabarnet road near Cheploch Gorge in the southern Kerio Valley, roughly 5 km west of the Chebloch Bridge. The college is purely agricultural, offering fully accredited TVET CDACC programmes from Level 3 to Level 5 in horticulture, dairy farm attendance, poultry production, sustainable agriculture, agriculture extension, agripreneurship, apiculture and integrated pest management, with trainees spending most of their time in hands-on learning on the centre''s 20-hectare demonstration farm. Supporting facilities include a conference centre with four halls and residential accommodation for 100 guests, a KEPHIS-certified tree nursery and a fruit processing factory supported by the Government of Japan, and the college publishes a student portal at students.catic.co.ke and a CDACC results portal at cdacc.catic.co.ke.","locked_by_verification":false},{"settled":true,"decision":"merge","rationale":"Auto-sync: deterministic non-destructive array/course union.","decided_at":"2026-11-21T12:14:31.557214+00:00","decided_by":"rule:auto-sync","field_path":"facilities","settled_at":"2026-11-21T12:14:31.557214+00:00","source_urls":["https://www.cheptebo.org/","https://www.cheptebo.org/contact.php","https://catic.co.ke/"],"merged_value":["20-hectare demonstration and training farm","Training and conference centre with four halls and residential accommodation for 100 guests","KEPHIS-certified tree nursery","Fruit processing factory supported by the Government of Japan","Training and conference centre with four conference halls","Residential accommodation for 100 guests with kitchen 