ocus on semi-arid areas, and which held its first graduation ceremony on 6 December 2026. The regulator''s accredited course table carries eighteen entries made up largely of duplicated CDACC rows; once duplicates are collapsed it resolves to nine accredited TVET CDACC qualifications spanning Levels 3 to 5: horticulture and poultry kienyeji operator at Level 3, agriculture extension at Level 4, and horticulture, integrated pest management, poultry breeding operations, sustainable agriculture for rural development, agripreneurship and apiculture at Level 5. The wider Cheptebo Rural Development Centre site, a ministry of the Africa Inland Church Kenya established in 1986, publishes a 20-hectare demonstration and training farm, a conference centre with four halls and residential accommodation for 100 guests, a KEPHIS-certified tree nursery and a fruit processing factory supported by the Government of Japan. No institutional email address or telephone number for the centre was confirmed from a page fetched in this run, and the imported town value was a plus-code string with no fetched corroboration, so both remain unverified.', '["20-hectare demonstration and training farm","Training and conference centre with four halls and residential accommodation for 100 guests","KEPHIS-certified tree nursery","Fruit processing factory supported by the Government of Japan","Training and conference centre with four conference halls","Residential accommodation for 100 guests with kitchen and dining facilities","Lecture halls and practical training on the demonstration farm"]', '["TVETA","TVET CDACC"]', '[{"name":"Agriculture and Extension Level 5","level":"Diploma","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Dairy Farm Attendance Level 3","level":"Artisan","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Dairy Farm Attendance Level 4","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"General Agriculture Level 4","level":"Certificate","exam_body":"TVET CDACC"},{"name":"Poultry Kienyeji Production Leve